-- title:
--   Kummer form of cyclic covers of the crossing model
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a complete (adically complete for its maximal ideal) discrete valuation domain, $\pi \in W$ irreducible, and $m, n$ positive integers such that $n$ and $mn$ are units in $W$ and such that $W$ contains a primitive $n$-th root of unity and a primitive $mn$-th root of unity. Write $R_0 =$ `UVCrossingModel W (π ^ (m * n))`, the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \pi^{mn}$. Let $K_0$ be a field realised as a fraction ring of $R_0$, and let $F$ be a field extension of $K_0$, compatibly an $R_0$-algebra, with $F/K_0$ finite Galois of cyclic Galois group and $[F : K_0] = n$. Let $B$ be the integral closure of $R_0$ in $F$; assume $B$ is local, that $B$ is unramified over $R_0$ at every prime $Q$ of $B$ whose contraction to $R_0$ has height $1$, and that every $b \in B$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $B$ to the image of `const (π ^ (m * n)) w` (the class of the constant power series $w$) for some $w \in W$. The conclusion is that there are a unit $u$ of $R_0$ and $\theta \in F$ with $\theta^n$ equal to the image in $F$ of $u \cdot$ `U (π ^ (m * n))`, and with $K_0(\theta) = F$.
--
--   This is the Kummer classification of cyclic covers of the crossing model $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1-\pi^{mn})$ that are unramified in height one and have rational closed point: such a cover is obtained by extracting an $n$-th root of a unit multiple of one of the crossing coordinates. It feeds the structural result [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_uvCrossingModel_pow_of_isGalois_of_isCyclic_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_residue_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_uvCrossingModel_pow_of_isGalois_of_isCyclic_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_residue_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul), identifying such covers with crossing models again, as in the local analysis of modular curves at crossing points of the special fibre.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_exists_pow_eq_unit_mul_U_of_isCyclic_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_residue_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul.lean

